# ── Line endings the tests depend on ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Measured on a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` (2026-10-13), where the
# blobs are LF but the working copy is CRLF:
#
#   • a shebang followed by CRLF is not stripped by vite's SSR transform, so the
#     module is loaded as `#!…` and V8 throws "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected
#     token" with no location. The suite does not fail — it never collects, and
#     the report says only "(0 test)". `scripts/audit-migration-ledger.mjs` did
#     exactly this.
#   • byte-for-byte goldens and the compose text the deployment guards parse were
#     compared against a CRLF working copy: 10 `dockerCompose` assertions and 5
#     `structuredReport/renderer` cases, red on this platform only, with the
#     clinical text identical apart from `\r`.
#
# These rules change only what a checkout writes; no blob is rewritten, and a
# Linux checkout (CI, the NAS) is already LF.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
**/__fixtures__/renderer/*.body.txt text eol=lf
